---
import AsterLayout from "../../layouts/AsterLayout.astro";
import { ASTER_DEX_ID, AUTHORS, PERSON_ID, SITE_URL } from "../../entity";
import { buildAsterPageGraph, buildBreadcrumbs } from "../../lib/schema";
import { ASTER_1001X_LADDER, ASTER_DOCS, ASTER_EXECUTION_FEES, ASTER_LAST_VERIFIED } from "../../data/aster";

const url = `${SITE_URL}/aster-dex/1001x/`;
const description =
  "How Aster's 1001x and Degen Mode work: the leverage ladder, the liquidation formula, the ROI caps, and why a 0.1% move can close a position.";

const articleNode = {
  "@type": "TechArticle",
  "@id": `${url}#article`,
  headline: "1001x",
  alternativeHeadline: "Aster 1001x: leverage, liquidation and the caps that matter",
  name: "Aster 1001x: leverage, liquidation and the caps that matter",
  description,
  url,
  mainEntityOfPage: url,
  inLanguage: "en",
  datePublished: "2026-11-24",
  dateModified: ASTER_LAST_VERIFIED,
  author: { "@id": AUTHORS.kirsty.id },
  editor: { "@id": AUTHORS.maksim.id },
  publisher: { "@id": PERSON_ID },
  isPartOf: { "@id": `${SITE_URL}/aster-dex/#collection` },
  articleSection: "Trading modes",
  about: [
    { "@id": ASTER_DEX_ID },
    { "@type": "Thing", name: "Leverage (finance)", sameAs: "https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1148384" },
    { "@type": "Thing", name: "Liquidation" },
  ],
  citation: [
    { "@type": "CreativeWork", name: "1001x leverage", url: `${ASTER_DOCS}trading/1001x/leverage` },
    { "@type": "CreativeWork", name: "1001x fees and slippage", url: `${ASTER_DOCS}trading/1001x/fees-and-slippage` },
    { "@type": "CreativeWork", name: "Degen Mode", url: `${ASTER_DOCS}trading/1001x/degen-mode` },
  ],
};

const breadcrumbs = buildBreadcrumbs(`${url}#breadcrumbs`, [
  { name: "Home", url: `${SITE_URL}/` },
  { name: "Aster DEX", url: `${SITE_URL}/aster-dex/` },
  { name: "1001x", url },
]);

const graph = buildAsterPageGraph([articleNode, breadcrumbs]);
---

<AsterLayout
  title="Aster 1001x — Leverage, Liquidation and ROI Caps | Maksim Sokal"
  description={description}
  canonical={url}
  graph={graph}
  trail={[{ label: "1001x" }]}
  modified={new Date(ASTER_LAST_VERIFIED)}
>
  <header class="space-y-5 max-w-3xl">
    <span class="text-xs font-mono text-sky-400 uppercase tracking-widest block">Trading Modes</span>
    <h1 class="font-display font-medium text-3xl md:text-4xl text-slate-100 tracking-tight leading-tight">
      1001x
    </h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
      1001x is Aster's onchain-liquidity perpetual mode. The headline is leverage up to 1001x on BTC/USD; the part that
      matters is how little price movement that implies before liquidation, and the caps that limit the upside.
    </p>
    <p class="text-[11px] font-mono text-slate-400">
      Verified <time datetime={ASTER_LAST_VERIFIED}>{ASTER_LAST_VERIFIED}</time> ·{" "}
      <a href={`${ASTER_DOCS}trading/1001x/leverage`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">official leverage docs</a>
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="space-y-4" aria-labelledby="ladder-heading">
    <h2 id="ladder-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-xl text-slate-100 tracking-tight">The leverage ladder</h2>
    <div class="space-y-3">
      {ASTER_1001X_LADDER.map((row) => (
        <div class="bg-brand-900/35 border border-[#1e293b]/60 rounded-xl p-5 space-y-2">
          <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2">
            <span class="text-sm text-slate-100 font-display">{row.market}</span>
            <span class="text-[11px] font-mono text-sky-300">max {row.maxLeverage}</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">{row.fees}</p>
          <p class="text-[11px] text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">{row.note}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4" aria-labelledby="degen-heading">
    <h2 id="degen-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-xl text-slate-100 tracking-tight">Degen Mode</h2>
    <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
      Degen Mode is the BTC/USD-only path for 500x, 750x and 1001x. It charges no opening fee, applies 0.01% slippage,
      and replaces the closing fee with a dynamic PnL-based fee with a 0.03% minimum. Margin cannot be added to an open
      position.
    </p>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-3">
      <div class="bg-brand-900/35 border border-[#1e293b]/60 rounded-xl p-4">
        <span class="block text-[10px] font-mono uppercase tracking-widest text-sky-400">Max net profit ROI</span>
        <span class="text-sm text-slate-100">≈500% at 500x / 750x</span>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-brand-900/35 border border-[#1e293b]/60 rounded-xl p-4">
        <span class="block text-[10px] font-mono uppercase tracking-widest text-sky-400">Max net profit ROI</span>
        <span class="text-sm text-slate-100">≈300% at 1001x</span>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-brand-900/35 border border-[#1e293b]/60 rounded-xl p-4">
        <span class="block text-[10px] font-mono uppercase tracking-widest text-sky-400">Slippage</span>
        <span class="text-sm text-slate-100">0.01% (BTC/USD)</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4" aria-labelledby="liq-heading">
    <h2 id="liq-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-xl text-slate-100 tracking-tight">Liquidation: the number that matters</h2>
    <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
      The docs give the distance to liquidation as:
    </p>
    <div class="bg-brand-950/60 border border-[#1e293b]/60 rounded-xl p-5">
      <code class="block text-xs text-sky-200 leading-relaxed">
        distance = entry × (initial margin × liquidation loss rate + cumulative funding) / initial margin / leverage
      </code>
    </div>
    <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
      Their worked example: entry $1,500, margin $100, funding $2, loss rate 85%, leverage 10x. The distance is $130.50
      and the liquidation price is $1,369.50.
    </p>
    <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
      Now change the leverage. At 1001x, a 0.1% adverse move is roughly the entire margin before fees and funding. The
      liquidation price sits next to the entry, which is why adding margin is disabled and why the ROI cap exists.
    </p>
    <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
      Funding is calculated every block in this mode and is reflected in unrealised PnL, so it moves the liquidation
      price continuously. A position that is not moving can still drift toward liquidation.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4" aria-labelledby="fees-heading">
    <h2 id="fees-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-xl text-slate-100 tracking-tight">Fees and execution</h2>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
      <div class="bg-brand-900/35 border border-[#1e293b]/60 rounded-xl p-5">
        <h3 class="font-display text-sm text-slate-100 mb-2">Below 500x</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">0.08% opening fee and 0.08% closing fee. Margin can be added.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-brand-900/35 border border-[#1e293b]/60 rounded-xl p-5">
        <h3 class="font-display text-sm text-slate-100 mb-2">500x and above</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">0% opening fee, dynamic PnL-based closing fee (minimum 0.03%), no added margin.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 text-[11px] font-mono text-slate-400">
      {ASTER_EXECUTION_FEES.map((row) => (
        <span>{row.chain}: <span class="text-slate-200">{row.fee}</span></span>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p class="text-[11px] text-slate-400">Execution fees apply on opening a position.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-rose-500/5 border border-rose-400/20 rounded-xl p-6 space-y-2" aria-labelledby="risk-heading">
    <h2 id="risk-heading" class="font-display font-medium text-sm text-rose-200 tracking-wide">Before you use it</h2>
    <ul class="space-y-2 text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed list-disc pl-5">
      <li>You can lose the full margin on a very small move.</li>
      <li>The profit upside is capped at roughly 300% at 1001x, even if price moves further.</li>
      <li>You cannot add margin at 500x or above; the position cannot be rescued by topping up.</li>
      <li>Funding accrues every block and changes the liquidation price.</li>
      <li>This mode is not available in restricted jurisdictions. See <a href="/aster-dex/eligibility/" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">eligibility</a>.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="border-t border-[#1e293b]/60 pt-6 space-y-2">
    <p class="text-[11px] text-slate-400">
      Written by <a href="/kirsty-moreland/" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">Kirsty Moreland</a> · Technical review by{" "}
      <a href="/about/" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">Maksim Sokal</a> ·
      <a href="/disclosure/" class="text-slate-400 hover:text-sky-300">Disclosure</a>
    </p>
    <p class="text-[11px] text-slate-400">
      Related: <a href="/aster-dex/shield-mode/" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">Shield Mode</a> ·
      <a href="/aster-dex/fees/" class="text-sky-400 hover:text-sky-300">fee schedule</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</AsterLayout>
